		{
			title: "Storing items"
			icon: {
				id: "appliedenergistics2:1k_storage_cell"
				Count: 1b
				tag: { }
			}
			x: 6.0d
			y: 8.0d
			subtitle: "Sorry for the wall of text"
			description: [
				"All cells have a mechanic called \"types\", that means they can store only 63 different kinds of items per cell. For example, 60 swords and 1 stack of cobblestone, dirt and gravel. "
				""
				"Unstackable items count as 1 item for 1 type. Stackable items count as a type only once, so you can put in 10 stacks of cobblestone and it only would be one type."
				""
				"The overall storage capacity of the cell depends on the number of used types."
				"For instance, you can put 8000 cobblestone on 1k storage cell if you use only 1 type. But if you already use 62 types, you can put only 4000 cobblestone on it."
				""
				"You can disassemble any empty cell by using shift + right click."
			]
			dependencies: ["4F6F1A457BF2EB1C"]
			id: "06768AAFC5CD6E42"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "49E78B29A3D293F9"
					type: "item"
					item: "appliedenergistics2:1k_cell_component"
				}
				{
